WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.360
Welcome to our video on Step 1 B of Send to Amazon, a streamlined shipment workflow that

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:12.520
saves you time by simplifying fulfillment by Amazon or FBA shipment creation.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:17.480
In this video, you'll learn steps to provide box content information and pack individual

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.560
units from Step 1 of the workflow.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.240
You won't see this step on Seller Central's Send to Amazon page if you already provided

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:32.520
box content information for all your SKUs using the case-pack templates in Step 1.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:38.000
Once you've confirmed the quantity of individual units to send to Amazon, we determine which

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.960
SKUs can be packed together based on whether they require special handling at our fulfillment

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:43.960
centers.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:49.640
For example, SKUs that are categorized as Dangerous Goods or Hazmat can't be packed

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.840
with other SKUs.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.160
That's because Dangerous Goods are shipped to special fulfillment centers that can receive

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.960
them safely.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:02.960
Two other factors that determine which SKUs can be packed together are product weights

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:04.240
and dimensions.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:09.440
Also, over-sized SKUs can't be packed with standard-sized SKUs.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:15.440
That's because over-sized SKUs can only be received at specialized fulfillment centers.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:20.520
Finally, SKUs that require prep or labeling to be performed by Amazon shouldn't be packed

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:23.480
with SKUs that are already prepped and labeled.

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:28.560
This ensures that boxes containing SKUs that don't require Amazon to prep or label them

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.960
aren't unnecessarily sidelined at the fulfillment center and can be made available to customers

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.840
sooner.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:40.360
Once your pack groups are determined, you'll be prompted to provide box content information

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.920
for the SKUs in each pack group.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:47.160
In this example, inventory has been sorted into two pack groups.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:50.640
You can pack SKUs in a pack group in any combination.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:56.280
However, you shouldn't mix SKUs from one pack group with SKUs from another pack group.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:01.960
If all units in a pack group fit into one box, select everything will fit into one box and

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:03.760
click Confirm.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:08.680
Then enter the box weight and dimensions and click Confirm Packing Information.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:13.440
If the units in a pack group will be packed in more than one box, select multiple boxes

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.800
will be needed and click Confirm.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:20.240
Next, provide packing information for your multiple boxes.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.400
From the drop down menu, you have three options.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:28.680
The enter through a web form option lets you enter box content information individually

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:30.680
using a web form.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:38.000
The Upload Excel File option lets you efficiently upload box content information in bulk.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:43.280
The Amazon Manually Processes Box Contents option lets you choose to outsource this step

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:48.000
and have Amazon provide this service for a per unit fee.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.640
Select enter through a web form if you have less than 12 units.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:56.400
Next, enter the estimated number of boxes and click Open Web Form.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.200
Then enter your box content information.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:04.160
Here, you'll enter the units boxed, box weight and box dimensions.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:07.160
Then click Confirm Packing Information.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:12.320
For more guidance, click Instructions or Need Help in the top right corner.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:17.920
Select Upload Excel File to efficiently upload box content information in bulk.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:23.720
Then enter the estimated number of boxes that the SKUs in a pack group will fit into.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.360
Next click Generate Excel File.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:29.440
Download the template and open the file in Excel.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:35.440
For each box, enter the number of units of each SKU that you'll be packing in that box.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:40.400
Make sure that the quantity of units in the boxes for each SKU is equal to the expected

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:43.560
quantity of SKUs in that box.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:46.160
Next enter the box weight and dimensions.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:53.740
As you pack, mark your boxes as Pack Group 1 Box 1, Pack Group 1 Box 2 and so on.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:59.320
This will help you match the right FBA Box ID label to each box in step 3, Print Box

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:00.960
Labels.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:04.840
After you're done packing your shipping boxes and entering the information in the Excel

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:12.040
file, save the file and upload it to Send to Amazon by clicking Upload and Validate File.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:16.840
We understand that as you pack your boxes, you might want to change the quantity of certain

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:24.280
SKUs to account for damaged inventory or to optimize the space inside one or more boxes.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:28.840
You can do so by going back to step 1 and updating the quantity of SKUs that you want

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:30.320
to send.

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:33.480
When you're done, proceed to step 1B.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:38.720
Note that the pack groups can change when you add or remove SKUs in step 1.

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:44.240
Make sure that you re-upload the box content information for updated pack groups.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:49.600
After you provide box content information for all pack groups, click Confirm and Continue

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:52.640
to proceed to the next step.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:58.240
This concludes the instructional video for step 1B, Pack Individual Units.

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:03.800
In the next step, we'll determine the optimal location for your boxes to be sent so they're as close

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:05.800
to your customers as possible.

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:10.600
Check out the video for step 2 Confirm Shipping in Seller University.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:13.520
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store.
